      "message": "I am hesitant to approve any `vertical-align: middle;`, because it does NOT do what you expect, which is center positioning.\n\nIf you want to center align multiple children, then the parent should be `display: flex` and `align-items: center`.\n\nIf you do that, then you probably also want to:\n\n* Remove `display: inline-block; vertical-align: top; position: relative; top: 8px;` here.\n* Wrap each child of the \u003cdiv\u003e flex parent with a \u003cdiv\u003e, because flex children cannot be `display: inline` and it is a source of confusion when `\u003cspan\u003e` elements are treated as `display: block` or `display: inline...` rules are simply ignored by the browser.\n* Add a `flex-shrink: 0;` here, because otherwise the checkbox gets thinner when there is no space.",
